<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσις</span></b> , ὁ, poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσσις</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			6.323
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Leon.
		</span></i>); gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσιος</span> (no gen. is  found in 
			Att.
		, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσεως</span> only in Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.700
		</span></i>); dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πὁσει,</span>
		
			Ep.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσεϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.71
				</span></i>
			; voc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					323
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				913
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1399
				</span></i>
			: pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IA</u>
					176
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσιας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.240
				</span></i>
			:—<i>husband, spouse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.329
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Cypr.</u>
				93
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.99
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὁμοδέμνιον π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1108
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); esp. <i>lawful husband,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ π. μὲν Ἡρακλῆς ἐμὸς καλῆται, τῆς
					νεωτέρας δ᾽ ἀνήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					550
				</span></i>
			 (but cf.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.725
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				763
			</span></i>): rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1335b41
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ ἄλοχος</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1253b6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρυπτὸς π.,</span> of a paramour,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				561
			</span></i>. (I.-<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>potis</i> 'lord, master', cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πότνια,
				δεσπότης,</span> Skt.<i>pátis</i> 'lord,
			master, husband', <i>pátnī</i> 'lady, wife',
			Lat. <i>potis</i> (<i>sum</i>), etc.)</div>
